course: dictionary
lesson: 8303
title: Short forms and fragments
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «ro» is not a word you can use in a sentence on its own. It is a short form, called an abbreviation, or a piece cut from a longer word. When you meet it, look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «RO» is short for «reverse osmosis», a way of cleaning water by pushing it through a very fine filter. You may see «RO water» on a water filter or bottle. In a science lesson about water, reverse osmosis can help make sea water safe to drink.
explain: On a computer, «.ro» at the end of a web address shows a Romanian website. This «ro» is the code for Romania and the Romanian language. Sometimes «ro» is just a piece of a longer word, such as «robot». Context tells you which one you have.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or phrase.
fact: «RO» means «reverse osmosis», a way of cleaning water by pushing it through a very fine filter.
fact: «.ro» at the end of a web address shows a Romanian website, and «ro» is the code for Romania and the Romanian language.
fact: «ro» is often just a piece of a longer word, such as «robot» or «row».
exercise: In a science lesson, «RO water» is water cleaned by what? | Adding sugar to it | *Reverse osmosis | Freezing it in ice | Boiling it in a pan
exercise: Ella sees the web address «news.ro». What does «.ro» show? | A shop that sells rolls | A website about water filters | *A Romanian website | A robot maker
exercise: Which is a longer word with «ro» as just one piece of it? | RO | *robot | .ro | lamp
test: In a web address ending «.ro», what does «.ro» tell you? | A water filter | *A Romanian website | A shop that sells rolls | A robot maker
test: What does «RO» stand for on a water bottle? | Round object | Really old | Roast onion | *Reverse osmosis
exam: Max sees «ro» in a book and does not know it. What is the best first step? | Stop reading and give up | *Read the words around it to find clues, then check a dictionary | Skip the whole book forever | Guess that it means dog
